---
/**
 * VoiceHero - Main homepage hero. Eyebrow, H1 with ink-block highlight,
 * tagline, description, install CTA. Centered.
 *
 * Mirrors handoff Hero.jsx VoiceHero. Topology renders inside (step 4).
 */
import Container from "@/components/ui/container.astro";
import H1 from "@/components/ui/typography-h1.astro";
import P from "@/components/ui/typography-p.astro";
import Small from "@/components/ui/typography-small.astro";
import InkBlock from "@/components/InkBlock.astro";
import HeroInstallCTA from "@/components/HeroInstallCTA.astro";
import HeroTopology from "@/components/HeroTopology.astro";
---

<section class="border-b border-border">
    <Container size="5xl" padding="20" gap="10" class="items-center text-center">
        <Small color="muted-foreground" transform="uppercase" tracking="widest">
            sqlite sync engine &middot; one rust binary &middot; mit
        </Small>

        <H1 align="center" size="7xl" weight="bold">
            If you're moving SQLite, <InkBlock>smuggl</InkBlock> it.
        </H1>

        <P align="center" size="display-small" class="max-w-prose">
            SQLite to SQLite. LAN UDP multicast. S3 relay. Turso, rqlite, Datasette, StarbaseDB, SQLite Cloud, and D1 once its three open defects land. One binary, plus one plugin.
        </P>

        <HeroTopology />

        <P align="center" color="muted-foreground" class="max-w-prose">
            Nothing else combines these shapes in a single tool. Litestream does S3 backup. rqlite does Raft. ElectricSQL needs a server. smugglr does local, LAN, relay, and hosted backend: content-hashed delta sync, no coordinator, no service to run.
        </P>

        <div class="w-full max-w-xl">
            <HeroInstallCTA
                command="curl -fsSL https://smugglr.dev/install | bash"
                subline="Installs the checksum-verified binaries on macOS and Linux x64. On Windows, use cargo install smugglr and cargo install smugglr-http-sql, or the release zip."
            />
        </div>
    </Container>
</section>
